=== SPLIT-CLASSIFICATION HUNT (recurring defect class 1) === CLEAN

Enumerated every surface that could re-implement pending/posted pairing rather
than trusting the diff:
  grep -rn "isCandidatePair|detectNearDuplicatePairs|isPendingPostedPair|isPendingStatus|isPostedStatus|commonPrefixLen|postedStatusKeywords" --include=*.go internal/ cmd/
  grep -rniE "pending" --include=*.go internal/ cmd/ (excluding spending/depending)
  grep -rniE "pending" web/templates web/static/js
Results:
- pendingPostedWindowDays and pendingPostedPrefixMinLen appear ONLY in
  internal/services/dataloader/near_duplicates.go (lines 20-33 defs, 209/228
  uses). No second threshold anywhere.
- postedStatusKeywords is referenced only in near_duplicates.go (lines 46, 248,
  285). isPendingStatus/isPostedStatus have no callers outside that file.
- detectNearDuplicatePairs has exactly one production caller:
  internal/services/dataloader/loader.go:1020. The Duplicates page and the MCP
  tools read the resulting queue; none re-derives pending/posted pairing.
- internal/services/transfers/transfers.go has its own unexported
  isCandidatePair, but it is transfer-leg matching (pre-existing, no Status /
  pending-posted logic) — a name collision, not a second classifier.
- web/templates and web/static/js: the only "pending" hits are
  whatif-pending-card (a loading skeleton) and whatifChartsReloadPending (a JS
  flag). No client-side duplicate classification.
- The greedy loop's own window is untouched: duplicateWindowDays = 7 at line 18
  and the loop test `if diff < 0 || diff > duplicateWindowDays` at line 118 are
  unchanged in the diff; the 3-day rule is self-enforced inside
  isPendingPostedPair (line 209), exactly as the spec required.
- dayDiff (line 307) takes the absolute difference, so the window is
  order-independent.
